# Deploying to the defence Kubernetes cluster

"Deploy to defence k8s / defence cluster / dev161" always means this target and
nothing else:

| | |
|---|---|
| App URL | https://jeen-insights.dev161.internal/ (private DNS A record → internal `approuting-istio` Gateway; HTTP redirects to HTTPS) |
| Cluster | AKS `aks-openmetadata-dev161-weu`, kube context `defence-aks-openmetadata-dev161` |
| Namespace / release | `jeen-insights` / Helm release `jeen-insights` from `deployment/k8s_dev` |
| Overlay | `deployment/k8s_dev/values.defence.yaml` (Recreate strategy, `role=apps` node pool, Gateway API) |
| Registry | `acrjeendefensedev30fff5c1.azurecr.io/jeen-insights/jeen-insights-{api,ui,analytics}` |
| Secrets | hand-managed `jeen-insights-secrets`, ConfigMap `jeen-insights-idp-ca`, and self-signed TLS certificate/key synced from `kv-jeen-defense-dev-30ff`; never templated |
| Metadata DB | `10.42.2.4` `jeen_data_metadata`, shared with the LIVE Schema Modeler — Insights-owned objects only |
| DNS zone | private zone `dev161.internal` in RG `cts-dev-metadata-environment` |

## Procedure

1. Before a TLS cutover, confirm Key Vault secrets `jeen-insights-tls-crt` and
   `jeen-insights-tls-key` exist, the certificate SAN contains
   `jeen-insights.dev161.internal`, and the private key matches the certificate.
   This certificate is self-signed like the dashboard certificate, so browsers
   warn unless it is explicitly installed as trusted. The Gateway reserves
   private IP `10.42.6.19`.
2. Build **linux/amd64** images from the working tree with an immutable tag
   `$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M)-$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)`; `az acr login` then push.
   Only rebuild the components whose code changed; keep the other tags.
3. Schema changes go through the chart's disabled-by-default, non-hook Job,
   never through pods. Render only that template, then apply/wait/log it:
   `helm template jeen-insights deployment/k8s_dev --namespace jeen-insights --values deployment/k8s_dev/values.defence.yaml --values deployment/k8s_dev/values.migration.example.yaml --set-string migration.bundleId=<dns-safe-immutable-id> --set-string migration.image.repository=acrjeendefensedev30fff5c1.azurecr.io/jeen-insights/jeen-insights-api --set-string migration.image.tag=<api-tag> --set-string migration.existingSecret.name=jeen-insights-secrets --show-only templates/migration-job.yaml > /tmp/jeen-insights-migration.yaml`;
   `kubectl --context defence-aks-openmetadata-dev161 --namespace jeen-insights apply -f /tmp/jeen-insights-migration.yaml`;
   `kubectl --context defence-aks-openmetadata-dev161 --namespace jeen-insights wait --for=condition=complete job/jeen-insights-migrate-<dns-safe-immutable-id> --timeout=15m`;
   `kubectl --context defence-aks-openmetadata-dev161 --namespace jeen-insights logs job/jeen-insights-migrate-<dns-safe-immutable-id>`.
   Review success before upgrading workloads. Pods run with both
   `RUN_MIGRATIONS_ON_START=false` and `SCHEMA_BOOTSTRAP_ON_START=false` and
   refuse to start if the baseline is missing.
4. `helm dependency build deployment/k8s_dev` (the packaged subcharts go stale
   when a chart template changes). For the first TLS cutover only, retain the
   old UI LoadBalancer and HTTP runtime values with temporary `--set` overrides
   while installing the Gateway. Verify the new endpoint before changing DNS:
   `curl --resolve jeen-insights.dev161.internal:443:10.42.6.19 https://jeen-insights.dev161.internal/health`.
   Register the HTTPS Keycloak and Zitadel callback URLs, update the private DNS
   A record to `10.42.6.19`, then run the final upgrade without temporary
   overrides:
   `helm upgrade --install jeen-insights deployment/k8s_dev --kube-context defence-aks-openmetadata-dev161 --namespace jeen-insights --values deployment/k8s_dev/values.defence.yaml --set jeen-insights-api.image.tag=… --set jeen-insights-ui.image.tag=… --set jeen-insights-analytics.image.tag=… --rollback-on-failure --wait --timeout 10m`.
5. Verify: pods Ready; Gateway and both HTTPRoutes are accepted; the API log
   shows `baseline verified`, `model=gpt-5.1`, `DB catalog mode`;
   `curl -I http://jeen-insights.dev161.internal/` returns a 301 to HTTPS;
   `curl --insecure https://jeen-insights.dev161.internal/health` succeeds and
   the served certificate has the expected fingerprint; then
   `cd tests/e2e && LIVE_APP_URL=https://jeen-insights.dev161.internal LIVE_EMAIL=live-admin LIVE_PASSWORD=… npm run test:live:smoke`.

## Do not

- Point anything at the dev stack (`jeen-dev-db…`, `jeen-ai-dev-swe…`) — the
  defence overlay leaves `AZURE_OPENAI_*` blank on purpose; the model comes from
  the DB (`gpt-5.1` on `jeen-ai-defense-dev-swe`).
- Touch Schema Modeler tables (`metadata_*`, `settings_services`, `admin_*`, …)
  from migrations or fixes; only `insights_*`, `connector*`, `auth_users`, `app_settings`.
- Run `RUN_MIGRATIONS_ON_START=true` or DDL from an API pod against this DB.
